   1:../Src/music.c **** /**
   2:../Src/music.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:../Src/music.c ****   * @file    music.c
   4:../Src/music.c ****   * @author  MCU Application Team
   5:../Src/music.c ****   * @brief   PWM-DAC speech/music player with 6-band equaliser
   6:../Src/music.c ****   *          (TIM1_CH2/CH2N complementary PWM, pins PA9/PA12).
   7:../Src/music.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   8:../Src/music.c ****   * @attention
   9:../Src/music.c ****   *
  10:../Src/music.c ****   * Playback chain
  11:../Src/music.c ****   * --------------
  12:../Src/music.c ****   *   platform_pcm.c (8 bit PCM, 16 kHz, EQ'd offline by tools/wav2pcm.py)
  13:../Src/music.c ****   *        |
  14:../Src/music.c ****   *   [runtime 6-band EQ, RBJ biquads in Q15]     <- MUSIC_EqSetBand()
  15:../Src/music.c ****   *        |
  16:../Src/music.c ****   *   [PWM DAC] TIM1_CH2/CH2N, carrier ~62.5 kHz, duty = sample
  17:../Src/music.c ****   *        |
  18:../Src/music.c ****   *   piezo buzzer between PA9 and PA12 (differential drive = 2x swing)
  19:../Src/music.c ****   *
  20:../Src/music.c ****   * Two EQ layers cooperate:
  21:../Src/music.c ****   *  - the offline EQ (tools/wav2pcm.py --eq) does the heavy, static speech
  22:../Src/music.c ****   *    shaping while generating the data;
  23:../Src/music.c ****   *  - the runtime EQ below refines it on the target without regenerating
  24:../Src/music.c ****   *    anything. Both use the same band layout (MUSIC_EQ_BAND_DEFS in
  25:../Src/music.c ****   *    music.h): -6 dB shelf below 200 Hz, +3/+2 dB vowel body at 300/900 Hz,
  26:../Src/music.c ****   *    +5/+3 dB consonants/presence at 2.5/3.5 kHz, -6 dB shelf above 6 kHz.
  27:../Src/music.c ****   *
  28:../Src/music.c ****   * Sample pacing: TIM2 fires one update interrupt per PCM sample at
  29:../Src/music.c ****   * PLATFORM_PCM_RATE_HZ (16 kHz). The ISR runs the 6 biquads on one sample
ARM GAS  C:\Users\n11ak\AppData\Local\Temp\ccneynBe.s 			page 2


  30:../Src/music.c ****   * (42 int32 MACs) and latches the duty - comfortably inside the 64 us
  31:../Src/music.c ****   * sample period at 16 MHz.
  32:../Src/music.c ****   *
  33:../Src/music.c ****   * Pin mapping: PA9 = TIM1_CH2, PA12 = TIM1_CH2N (AF6). No dead time is set:
  34:../Src/music.c ****   * the complementary pair here forms a differential drive of one piezo
  35:../Src/music.c ****   * element, not a half bridge.
  36:../Src/music.c ****   ******************************************************************************
  37:../Src/music.c ****   * This software component is licensed under BSD 3-Clause license.
  38:../Src/music.c ****   ******************************************************************************
  39:../Src/music.c ****   */
  40:../Src/music.c **** 
